%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: types of TEP
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: The Bachelor of Elementary Education (B.El.Ed.) program is structurally
      classified as what type of program?
    Options:
    - A consecutive model program
    - An in-service teacher education program
    - An integrated teacher education program
    - A special education program
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: If a policy planner aims to reduce the total time taken to become
      a qualified secondary teacher while ensuring deeper integration of subject
      knowledge and pedagogy, which program type should they advocate for?
    Options:
    - The consecutive B.Ed. model
    - "The 4-year integrated B.A. B.Ed./B.Sc.\_B.Ed. model"
    - A series of short-term in-service workshops
    - The Diploma in Elementary Education (D.El.Ed.)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: What is the primary distinction between pre-service and in-service
      teacher education?
    Options:
    - Pre-service is for secondary teachers, in-service is for elementary teachers.
    - Pre-service is theoretical, in-service is practical.
    - Pre-service is qualification-oriented for new entrants, while in-service provides
      continuous professional development for working teachers.
    - Pre-service is offered by universities, in-service is offered by NGOs.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher with a B.Ed. degree undergoes a 3-week training on implementing
      experiential learning. This activity is an example of:'
    Options:
    - Pre-service teacher education
    - In-service teacher education
    - An integrated program
    - A consecutive program
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: The National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 recommends phasing out
      which of the following structures for teacher preparation?
    Options:
    - Integrated 4-year programs
    - The 2-year B.Ed. program
    - The 1-year B.Ed. program
    - Master of Education (M.Ed.) programs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A program designed to equip teachers with specialized skills for
      teaching students with visual impairments is categorized under:'
    Options:
    - Elementary Teacher Education
    - Physical Education
    - Adult Education
    - Special Education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: The 'consecutive model' of teacher education is best described
      by which of the following pathways?
    Options:
    - B.A. B.Ed. (4-year integrated program)
    - "B.Sc.\_\u2192 B.Ed. (Two separate degrees)"
    - "D.El.Ed. \u2192 B.Ed."
    - "B.Ed. \u2192 M.Ed."
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'Critically analyze the following scenario: A B.Ed. college introduces
      a mandatory module where student-teachers must develop a digital portfolio
      of their lesson plans and student work. This innovation primarily addresses
      a limitation of which traditional program characteristic?'
    Options:
    - Overemphasis on theoretical foundations
    - Lack of a reflective practice component
    - Insufficient focus on physical education
    - Absence of a consecutive model structure
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is the foundational pre-service qualification
      for teaching at the secondary level (Classes 9-10) in India?
    Options:
    - Diploma in Elementary Education (D.El.Ed.)
    - Bachelor of Physical Education (B.P.Ed.)
    - Master of Education (M.Ed.)
    - Bachelor of Education (B.Ed.)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: Imagine two teacher education programs. Program A is a 4-year B.A.
      B.Ed. Program B is a 3-year B.A. followed by a 2-year B.Ed. Which of the following
      is a potential advantage of Program A over Program B?
    Options:
    - It takes longer to complete.
    - It allows for a deeper, more simultaneous integration of disciplinary knowledge
      and pedagogical principles.
    - It is a consecutive model.
    - It focuses only on pedagogy and not on subject content.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: The Diploma in Elementary Education (D.El.Ed.) is primarily designed
      to prepare teachers for which stage of schooling?
    Options:
    - Pre-primary and Nursery
    - Classes I to VIII (Elementary Stage)
    - Classes IX and X (Secondary Stage)
    - Classes XI and XII (Senior Secondary Stage)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: Which regulatory body is responsible for recognizing and regulating
      teacher education programs like B.Ed. and D.El.Ed. in India?
    Options:
    - University Grants Commission (UGC)
    - National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)
    - National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE)
    - Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A B.P.Ed. graduate is qualified to:'
    Options:
    - Teach science at the secondary level.
    - Serve as a special educator for children with learning disabilities.
    - Become a principal of a senior secondary school.
    - Teach physical education in schools.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The M.Ed. program is best described as a:'
    Options:
    - Pre-service program for secondary teachers.
    - Pre-service program for elementary teachers.
    - Higher-degree program for teacher educators and educational specialists.
    - Diploma program for in-service training.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: What is the primary goal of in-service teacher education programs?
    Options:
    - To award a formal degree to aspiring teachers.
    - To provide a one-time orientation for new teachers.
    - To replace the need for pre-service qualifications.
    - To facilitate continuous professional development and updating of skills for
      practicing teachers.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The NISHTHA (National Initiative for School Heads'' and Teachers''
      Holistic Advancement) program launched by NCERT is a prime example of a:'
    Options:
    - Pre-service integrated program.
    - Large-scale in-service teacher training initiative.
    - Special education diploma program.
    - Consecutive model teacher education program.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher education program that includes a strong component of
      learning Indian Sign Language (ISL) is most likely a program in:'
    Options:
    - Early Childhood Education
    - Educational Technology
    - Special Education (Hearing Impairment)
    - Physical Education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The 2-year B.Ed. program, as mandated by NCTE, is an improvement
      over the 1-year program primarily because it:'
    Options:
    - Is more expensive to run.
    - Allows for an extended internship and more comprehensive coverage of pedagogical
      theory.
    - Focuses only on theoretical aspects.
    - Replaces the need for a master's degree.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: Which of the following sequences correctly represents the consecutive
      model of teacher education for a secondary school teacher?
    Options:
    - "B.El.Ed. \u2192 M.Ed."
    - "D.El.Ed. \u2192 B.Ed."
    - Integrated B.A. B.Ed.
    - "B.A. \u2192 B.Ed."
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A key philosophical difference between an integrated B.El.Ed.
      and a consecutive B.Ed. is that the integrated model:'
    Options:
    - Considers pedagogy and subject knowledge as separate domains to be mastered
      sequentially.
    - Views the development of a teacher's identity and professional knowledge as
      a simultaneous, intertwined process.
    - Is only for those who want to teach at the pre-primary level.
    - Eliminates the need for practical training.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: The Nursery Teacher Training (N.T.T.) program qualifies an individual
      to teach at which level?
    Options:
    - Senior Secondary Level (Classes 11-12)
    - Elementary Level (Classes 1-8)
    - Pre-Primary / Early Childhood Level
    - Secondary Level (Classes 9-10)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A program that combines the study of history or science with the
      principles of teaching and learning within a single curriculum is known as
      a(n):'
    Options:
    - In-service program
    - Consecutive program
    - Special education program
    - Integrated program
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The Ph.D. in Education is primarily a:'
    Options:
    - Pre-service teacher qualification program.
    - Program for training school principals.
    - Research-focused degree for creating scholars and policy analysts.
    - Diploma in educational administration.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: If a state government wants to upgrade the qualifications of its
      existing elementary teachers who hold a D.El.Ed. to a degree level, which would
      be the most logical pathway to recommend?
    Options:
    - They must start over with a 4-year integrated B.El.Ed.
    - They can pursue a B.Ed. program designed for elementary teachers.
    - They should enroll in an M.Phil. program.
    - No further qualification is needed.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: The scope of teacher education programs includes training for which
      of the following?
    Options:
    - Only government school teachers.
    - Only those who wish to become school principals.
    - Only teachers in urban private schools.
    - Teachers for pre-primary, elementary, secondary, and senior secondary levels,
      including specialized areas.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a characteristic of a high-quality in-service
      teacher education program?
    Options:
    - It is a one-way lecture-based transmission of information.
    - It is directly linked to teachers' classroom contexts and challenges.
    - It has no connection to the current curriculum.
    - It is a one-time event at the beginning of a teacher's career.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The B.El.Ed. program places a strong emphasis on:'
    Options:
    - Advanced research methodologies.
    - Pedagogy suited for senior secondary education.
    - Child-centered learning and the context of elementary education.
    - The management of school finances.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher who completes an M.Ed. program is qualified to take
      up a position as a:'
    Options:
    - Physical Education teacher in a primary school.
    - Teacher educator in a B.Ed. college.
    - Nursery school teacher.
    - Secondary school science teacher.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: The "reflective teaching practice" is a core component most effectively
      integrated into which type of program?
    Options:
    - A short-term 10-day orientation program
    - A correspondence course with no practical component
    - A program focused solely on theoretical examinations
    - A program with a sustained and supervised internship period, like the 2-year
      B.Ed.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: What is a major challenge faced by the in-service teacher education
      system in India?
    Options:
    - They are the only pathway to become a teacher.
    - They are often disconnected from classroom realities and fail to bring about
      tangible changes in teaching practices.
    - They are mandatory for obtaining a Ph.D.
    - They replace pre-service qualifications.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: The D.El.Ed. program is typically of how many years' duration?
    Options:
    - 1 year
    - 2 years
    - 4 years
    - 6 months
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A program that leads to a Bachelor of Physical Education degree
      is abbreviated as:'
    Options:
    - B.P.Ed.
    - B.Ed.
    - B.El.Ed.
    - D.P.Ed.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The Integrated Teacher Education Programme (ITEP) as envisioned
      in NEP 2020 will be offered in:'
    Options:
    - IITs and IIMs only.
    - Multi-disciplinary colleges and universities.
    - Industrial training institutes.
    - Secondary schools only.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A key difference between the B.Ed. and the M.Ed. program is that
      the M.Ed. focuses more on:'
    Options:
    - Basic classroom teaching skills.
    - Preparing teachers for the elementary level.
    - Educational research, leadership, and teacher education.
    - Foundational literacy and numeracy.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The ''Sandwich'' pattern of teacher education sometimes used in
      B.Ed. programs refers to:'
    Options:
    - A program that includes free meals for students.
    - Alternating blocks of theoretical coursework and school-based internship.
    - A program that focuses only on summer vacations.
    - A course on food nutrition for teachers.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'Evaluating the effectiveness of a teacher education program should
      ideally involve assessing:'
    Options:
    - Only the final university examination scores of the student-teachers.
    - The cost of the program.
    - The number of books in the institution's library.
    - The ability of the graduating teachers to foster student learning in real classrooms.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The Post-Graduate Diploma in Educational Management (PGDEM) is
      designed for:'
    Options:
    - Nursery teachers.
    - Aspiring educational administrators and leaders.
    - Special educators for children with autism.
    - Physical education trainers.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A pre-service teacher education program that is considered ''job-oriented''
      inherently implies that it:'
    Options:
    - Guarantees a government job.
    - Is the same as a Bachelor of Arts degree.
    - Is only about theoretical knowledge.
    - Focuses on developing specific competencies required for the teaching profession.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The District Institute of Education and Training (DIET) primarily
      focuses on:'
    Options:
    - Offering Ph.D. programs in education.
    - Providing in-service training for elementary teachers and teacher educators
      at the district level.
    - Regulating university-level B.Ed. programs.
    - Training teachers for foreign countries.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: A critique of the traditional 1-year B.Ed. program was that its
      internship was often too brief and perfunctory. How does the 2-year B.Ed. program
      address this?
    Options:
    - By removing the internship component entirely.
    - By providing a longer, more substantial and supervised school experience.
    - By focusing only on theoretical coursework.
    - By converting it into a correspondence course.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: What is the primary focus of Early Childhood Care and Education
      (ECCE) teacher training programs?
    Options:
    - Preparing teachers for senior secondary classes.
    - Educational administration and management.
    - Advanced pedagogical theory for subject teachers.
    - The holistic development of children in the 3-6 years age group through play
      and discovery.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The M.Phil. (Master of Philosophy) in Education was a program
      that:'
    Options:
    - Served as a pre-doctoral research degree.
    - Was the basic qualification for primary teaching.
    - Focused solely on physical training.
    - Was a diploma in nursery education.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher education program that includes courses on "Braille"
      and "Orientation & Mobility" is designed for:'
    Options:
    - Teaching Physical Education.
    - Special Education for children with Visual Impairment.
    - Teaching Mathematics at the secondary level.
    - Early Childhood Education.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The National Curriculum Framework for Teacher Education (NCFTE,
      2009) emphasized making teacher education more ''integrated''. This was a direct
      critique of the:'
    Options:
    - High cost of education.
    - Overemphasis on practical training.
    - Lack of buildings for teacher education institutions.
    - Artificial separation between theory and practice in traditional programs.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A ''bridge course'' in the context of teacher education is often
      designed to:'
    Options:
    - Help teachers learn how to construct physical bridges.
    - Provide a pathway for teachers with one qualification (e.g., D.El.Ed.) to upgrade
      to another (e.g., B.Ed.).
    - Replace the B.Ed. degree entirely.
    - Train teachers for engineering colleges.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The B.Ed. (Special Education) program is typically offered for
      various disabilities. This specialization is crucial because:'
    Options:
    - It is easier to complete than a general B.Ed.
    - It has no practical component.
    - It allows teachers to avoid mainstream classrooms.
    - It equips teachers with specific strategies to address the diverse learning
      needs of children with disabilities.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: The 'understanding level' of teaching is a key objective of which
      type of teacher education program?
    Options:
    - Only pre-service programs
    - Only in-service programs
    - All quality teacher education programs, both pre-service and in-service
    - Only physical education programs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'A significant advantage of distance or online in-service teacher
      education programs is their:'
    Options:
    - Ability to provide hands-on practical training.
    - Potential to reach a large number of teachers across geographical barriers.
    - Replacement of all face-to-face interaction.
    - Focus solely on theoretical research.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'The Justice J.S. Verma Committee (2012) was constituted to review
      and revitalize:'
    Options:
    - The infrastructure of schools in India.
    - The sports policy of India.
    - The curriculum for medical education.
    - Teacher education in India.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: types of TEP
  - QuestionText: 'When comparing a 4-year integrated B.A. B.Ed. with a 3-year B.A.
      + 2-year B.Ed. pathway, a potential drawback of the integrated program could
      be:'
    Options:
    - It is more time-efficient.
    - A student must commit to the teaching profession at the entry point of undergraduate
      studies itself.
    - It provides a richer integration of content and pedagogy.
    - It is recommended by the NEP 2020.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: types of TEP
